Recommends: gir1.2-gtk-4.0,
            gir1.2-adw-1,
            python3-gi
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: Focus tool that blocks websites and applications
 Anchor blocks websites and applications during focus sessions, enforces
 breaks, and runs sessions on weekly schedules. A block cannot be undone in a
 moment of weakness: leaving early costs time and effort, and every escape is
 recorded.
 .
 Anchor provides friction, not guarantees. Anyone with root on the machine can
 defeat it; the goal is that doing so is tedious and leaves a record.
 .
 The graphical interface needs GTK4 and libadwaita, which are recommended
 rather than required so that a server install stays small. The top-bar
 indicator speaks StatusNotifierItem over D-Bus directly (see docs/adr/0003),
 so no AppIndicator library is needed; on GNOME it wants the AppIndicator
 shell extension, which Ubuntu enables by default.
